The action of the orthogonal group $O\left(  2r,\mathbb{R}\right)  $ on
$\mathcal{F}$ is given by cannonical transformations, which are given by the
adjoint representation of $O\left(  2r,\mathbb{R}\right)  $ on $\mathcal{F}%
_{1}$ leading to
\begin{equation}
\widehat{u}\left(  g\right)  \left(  A\right)  =u\left(  g\right)  ^{\dagger
}Au\left(  g\right)  ,
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
