{}\right\vert \right)  _{p,q}$ that are selfadjoint and nilpotent
\begin{align}
\nu_{j}  &  =\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(  x_{j}+x_{j+\max\left(  p,q\right)
/2}\right) \\
\left(  \nu_{j}\right)  ^{2}  &  =\frac{1}{2}\left(  x_{j}+x_{j+\max\left(
p,q\right)  /2}\right)  \left(  x_{j}+x_{j+\max\left(  p,q\right)  /2}\right)
=0\\
