\subsubsection{General form}

Any one particle operator $\lambda_{1}$ can be expressed as
\begin{align}
\lambda_{1}  &  =\sum_{1\leq j,k\leq r}\lambda_{1jk}a_{j}^{\dagger}a_{k}%
=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{1\leq j,k\leq r}\lambda_{1jk}\left(  x_{j}-ix_{j+r}\right)
\left(  x_{k}+ix_{k+r}\right) \nonumber\\
&  =\frac{1}{2}\sum_{1\leq j,k\leq r}\lambda_{1jk}\left\{  x_{j}x_{k}%
+x_{j+r}x_{k+r}+ix_{j}x_{k+r}-ix_{j+r}x_{k}\right\}  ,
\end{align}
which can be further developed as
\begin{align}
\lambda_{1}  &  =\frac{1}{2}\left(  \operatorname*{Tr}\lambda_{1}\right)
I_{\mathcal{F}}+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{1\leq j<k\leq r}\left(  \lambda_{1jk}%
